HYBRID_RESULT {"hybrid": "H02", "parents": ["S02", "S03"], "synthesis": "**Integrated Technical Memory for AX-731 Cross-Domain Mechanical-Software Relations Engineering Synthesis**\n\n### Mechanical Specifications\n- **Actuator Output Torque**: 12 newton meters. [C04]\n- **Gearbox Reduction Ratio**: 5 to 1. [C05]\n- **Maximum Mechanical Axis Speed**: 1200 rpm. [C06]\n\n### Software Specifications\n- **Sampling Interval**: The AX-731 PLC samples the drive current every 10 milliseconds. [C07]\n- **Fault Code F17**: The fault code F17 is raised when the AX-731 drive current exceeds 24 amperes. [C08]\n- **Reset Procedure for F17**: After fault F17 is triggered, a manual reset is required. This reset should only be performed after the drive current has returned to a level below the threshold", "readouts": [{"id": "S02", "raw": "The AX-731 mechanical technical specifications, numbers, and conditions available in the memory are as follows:\n\n- **Actuator Output Torque**: 12 newton meters. [C04]\n- **Gearbox Reduction Ratio**: 5 to 1. [C05]\n- **Maximum Mechanical Axis Speed**: 1200 rpm. [C06]\n\n**Deductions**:\n- Given the gearbox reduction ratio of 5 to 1, the input speed to the gearbox must be higher than the output speed. If the maximum mechanical axis speed (output speed) is 1200 rpm, the input speed to the gearbox would be 1200 rpm * 5 = 6000 rpm. However, this deduction is not explicitly stated in the provided information.", "question": "List all AX-731 mechanical technical specifications, numbers and conditions in the available memory.", "role": "domain"}, {"id": "S03", "raw": "The technical specifications, numbers, and conditions for the AX-731 software, as available in the memory, are as follows:\n\n- **Sampling Interval**: The AX-731 PLC samples the drive current every 10 milliseconds. [C07]\n- **Fault Code F17**: The fault code F17 is raised when the AX-731 drive current exceeds 24 amperes. [C08]\n- **Reset Procedure for F17**: After fault F17 is triggered, a 